# Walkthrough: Backend Restructuring for Microservices

The `backend` has been successfully restructured from a monolithic directory into a modular monorepo using NPM workspaces. This separation allows the Personal and Enterprise features to be developed, scaled, and deployed independently while sharing a common core and set of utilities.

## Refined Directory Structure

The project now follows this hierarchy:

```text
backend/
├── apps/
│   ├── enterprise/         # ERP Service (Port 5000)
│   │   ├── src/
│   │   │   ├── modules/    # Finance, Sales, Inventory, CRM, etc.
│   │   │   ├── app.ts      # Tailored for Enterprise modules
│   │   │   └── server.ts
│   │   └── package.json
│   └── personal/           # Personal Finance Service (Port 5001)
│       ├── src/
│       │   ├── modules/    # Expense, SMS Tracker
│       │   ├── app.ts      # Tailored for Personal modules
│       │   └── server.ts
│       └── package.json
├── packages/
│   ├── core/               # Shared Business Logic & Auth
│   │   └── src/modules/core/
│   └── shared/             # Shared Infrastructure (Config, Utils, Middlewares)
│       └── src/            # config/, middlewares/, repositories/, etc.
├── package.json            # Root workspace configuration
└── tsconfig.base.json      # Shared TS aliases (@smarterp/core, @smarterp/shared)
```

## Key Changes Made

### 1. Workspace Initialization
- Configured `"workspaces": ["apps/*", "packages/*"]` in the root [package.json](file:///C:/Users/vigne/Project/30/ERP/backend/package.json).
- Initialized sub-packages with their own [package.json](file:///C:/Users/vigne/Project/30/ERP/backend/package.json) for name scoping (e.g., `@smarterp/enterprise-api`).

### 2. Module Migration
- **Enterprise ModulesMoved**: `finance`, `sales`, `inventory`, `purchase`, `crm`, `hr`, `marketing`, `agents`.
- **Personal Modules Moved**: `expense`, `sms-tracker`.
- **Architectural Cleanup**: Moved `core` logic to `/packages/core` and plumbings (`middlewares`, `utils`, `config`, `repositories`) to `/packages/shared`.

### 3. Import Refactoring
- Implemented `@smarterp/shared` and `@smarterp/core` aliases in [tsconfig.base.json](file:///C:/Users/vigne/Project/30/ERP/backend/tsconfig.base.json).
- Ran a comprehensive refactor script across all modules to update hundreds of relative imports (e.g., `../../../middlewares/` → `@smarterp/shared/middlewares/`).

### 4. Entry Point Independence
- **Enterprise App**: Configured to run on port 5000 with a dedicated daily cron job for payment reminders.
- **Personal App**: Configured to run on port 5001, providing a lightweight API for personal expense tracking.
- Both apps now use a standard [app.ts](file:///C:/Users/vigne/Project/30/ERP/backend/src/app.ts) / [server.ts](file:///C:/Users/vigne/Project/30/ERP/backend/server.ts) pattern tailored to their specific domains.

## How to Run

From the `backend` root, you can now run services individually using npm workspaces:

```bash
# Start Enterprise API
npm run dev --workspace=@smarterp/enterprise-api

# Start Personal API
npm run dev --workspace=@smarterp/personal-api
```

## Verification Results
- All legacy `src` files and redundant route files in the root have been removed.
- TypeScript configurations have been validated to ensure cross-workspace imports resolve correctly.
- Module boundaries are now enforced by the folder structure.
